Subject: ntdll: say when a native DLL is used instead of the builtin

Wine marks some builtins IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_PREFER_NATIVE, meaning "if a
native file is present, use that instead" -- a deliberate per-DLL judgement, and
often the right one. But applications install those files themselves: SSFIV runs
DXSETUP on first launch and drops 89 native DLLs into the prefix, xaudio2_7 among
them. From then on the application runs against an implementation this tree
neither builds nor tests, and the only record is a TRACE nobody has enabled.

That cost a debugging session here. A probe was compiled into the builtin
xaudio2_7 to answer whether the game reaches CreateMasteringVoice. It could never
fire -- the game had been loading the redistributed Microsoft DLL all along -- and
an empty log would have read as "the game does not use XAudio2".

Warn rather than override. Forcing builtin at this point would undo the upstream
judgement for every DLL at once, and native is the better answer for plenty of
them. The line names the DLL and how to try the builtin for one run.

At this hook it covers every DLL rather than a hand-maintained list, which
matters because each game installs its own redistributable. An earlier version of
this patch hooked get_load_order() instead and would never have fired at all:
the load order comes back as the plain default here, and the native preference is
decided later, in virtual_map_builtin_module.

On this bottle it names the three that are shadowed -- xaudio2_7, x3daudio1_7 and
xactengine3_7, all from the same DXSETUP run.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -4091,6 +4091,43 @@
     }
     else if (prefer_native && (image_info->dll_charact & IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_PREFER_NATIVE))
     {
+        /* The builtin is skipped because a native file is present and the builtin
+         * asks to yield to one -- upstream's per-DLL judgement, often right. But
+         * the application then runs against an implementation this tree neither
+         * builds nor tests, recorded only in a TRACE nobody has on, and
+         * applications install these themselves: SSFIV's DXSETUP drops 89 native
+         * DLLs into the prefix on first launch. A probe compiled into the builtin
+         * xaudio2_7 could never fire for exactly this reason, and the empty log
+         * nearly read as "the game does not use XAudio2".
+         *
+         * Warn, do not override: forcing builtin here would undo that judgement
+         * for every DLL at once. Once per module, best-effort. */
+        {
+            static WCHAR warned[32][64];
+            static unsigned int warned_count;
+            /* nt_name is a counted UNICODE_STRING and is NOT NUL-terminated, so
+             * the basename must be copied out before any wcs* call or
+             * debugstr_w reads it; printing it in place emitted the name
+             * followed by whatever happened to sit after it. */
+            WCHAR base[64];
+            unsigned int total = nt_name.Length / sizeof(WCHAR), off = 0, len, i;
+
+            for (i = 0; i < total; i++) if (nt_name.Buffer[i] == '\\') off = i + 1;
+            len = total - off;
+            if (len >= ARRAY_SIZE(base)) len = ARRAY_SIZE(base) - 1;
+            memcpy( base, nt_name.Buffer + off, len * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+            base[len] = 0;
+
+            for (i = 0; i < warned_count && i < ARRAY_SIZE(warned); i++)
+                if (!wcsicmp( warned[i], base )) break;
+            if (i == warned_count && warned_count < ARRAY_SIZE(warned))
+            {
+                wcscpy( warned[warned_count++], base );
+                ERR_(module)( "%s: using the NATIVE file, ignoring the builtin this "
+                              "tree ships. Set WINEDLLOVERRIDES=%s=b to compare.\n",
+                              debugstr_w(base), debugstr_w(base) );
+            }
+        }
         TRACE_(module)( "%s has prefer-native flag, ignoring builtin\n", debugstr_us(&nt_name) );
         status = STATUS_IMAGE_ALREADY_LOADED;
     }
